    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1846-a1">

                <pb facs="1355" n="1239" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1239"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Spencer to
                        General Edwards.</hi><anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d1846-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 637.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 20, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the letters to you from
                    Minister Price, under date of October 19 and November 19 last, with their
                    enclosures, regarding the disarmament of the National Police of Panama of large
                    arms, I have the honor to inform you that I am in receipt of an instruction from
                    the Department of State informing me that before giving further instructions in
                    the matter they wish me to obtain and report your views regarding Señor
                    Lefevre’s note, “particularly as to the claim made by him that the police are
                    now forbidden to make use of large arms in suppressing disturbances in the
                    cities of Panama and Colon.” This note referred to was sent by Mr. Price as an
                    enclosure in his letter, No. 601 of November 19, 1915, and I shall be glad to
                    transmit any reply you may care to make or any suggestions you might offer.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willing Spencer.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1846-f1" n="14" type="source" xml:id="d1846-f1-content">
                <p>The same to General Goethals, except the number, 638, and the number of the
                    letter referred to, 602.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
